### File format for profiles (example)

Create CSV files like `profile_A.csv`, `profile_B.csv` with headers and numeric rows:

```
x,torque,efficiency
0.0,0.0,0.75
10.0,5.5,0.78
20.0,11.2,0.80
30.0,18.0,0.82
...
```

`x` can be radius (kpc), rpm, time or any independent axis the curves share conceptually; the GUI will interpolate them onto a common grid for blending.

